n in `.claude.json`\n- User said about the other account: *\"I was not able to find my account but I have added the Nex live MCP in the main account Feroze Khan\"*\n- User member since August 25, 2026 on NexLev\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n1. **Researched NexLev MCP** — Found it's a free YouTube research MCP with 74 tools, uses OAuth, supports Claude/ChatGPT/Hermes/OpenClaw. No API key needed.\n\n2. **Added NexLev to Antigravity's MCP config** — Entry added to `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\mcp_config.json`:\n   ```json\n   \"nexlev\": {\n     \"serverUrl\": \"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\"\n   }\n   ```\n   **Result:** Server is reachable but returns `Unauthorized` — confirms OAuth is required.\n\n3. **Added NexLev to Claude Code CLI** — User ran: `claude mcp add -s user --transport http nexlev https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp`. Entry visible in `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.claude.json` at lines 882-886. Auth status: \"Needs authentication.\"\n\n4. **Discovered NexLev OAuth endpoints** from `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server`:\n   - Authorization: `https://auth.nexlev.io/authorize`\n   - Token: `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/mcp/oauth/token`\n   - Registration: `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/mcp/oauth/register`\n   - Supports: authorization_code, refresh_token, PKCE (S256)\n\n5. **Registered OAuth client** — Got `client_id: \"chatgpt-mcp-client\"` (NexLev returns the same client_id for all registrations). Redirect URIs include `http://localhost:19876/callback`.\n\n6. **Built Python OAuth flow script** at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexlev_oauth\\oauth_flow.py`. Multiple iterations to fix Windows URL mangling issue (Windows `cmd /c start` breaks URLs with `&` characters — fixed by using HTML redirect file).\n\n7. **Read NexLev quickstart docs** — Full markdown version at `https://dashboard.nexlev.io/docs-md/mcp/quickstart.md`. Key finding: Different endpoints for different platforms:\n   - Claude: `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp`\n   - ChatGPT/Codex: `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/mcp` or `/api/codex-mcp`\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### OAuth Flow Details\n- NexLev uses standard OAuth 2.0 with PKCE (S256)\n- `client_id` is always `chatgpt-mcp-client` regardless of what you register\n- Token endpoint auth method: `none` (no client secret needed)\n- Scopes: `openid profile email`\n- The OAuth flow REQUIRES browser interaction — user must log in and approve. Cannot be automated without browser control.\n\n### Failed Approaches\n1. **Direct SSE connection** — Adding `serverUrl` to `mcp_config.json` fails with `Unauthorized` because OAuth token is missing\n2. **`claude -p` non-interactive mode** — Does NOT trigger the OAuth browser flow. Just hangs waiting.\n3. **`claude mcp auth` command** — Does not exist. Auth only works via interactive `/mcp` command inside Claude Code REPL.\n4. **`cmd /c start` with long URLs** — Windows strips everything after `&` in URLs. Fixed by writing URL to HTML file with `<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\">` and opening the HTML file instead.\n5. **First OAuth script run timed out** — 5-minute timeout was too short. User approved at the exact moment it timed out. Extended to 10 minutes in final version.\n\n### Critical Architecture Notes\n- Antigravity supports **SSE transport** for remote MCP servers via `serverUrl` in `mcp_config.json`\n- Antigravity does NOT handle OAuth flows natively — it just sends requests to the URL\n- The plan (Option C) is: get OAuth token → build a local MCP proxy bridge (like the existing vidIQ bridge at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\vidiq_bridge\\vidiq_mcp_bridge.py`) → add the bridge to `mcp_config.json` as a stdio server\n- After getting the token, the bridge would forward requests to NexLev's API with the Bearer token in Authorization header\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\mcp_config.json`** — Added `nexlev` entry with `serverUrl` at line 35-37. File has 55 lines total. Contains all MCP server configs including vidiq, notebooks, visualization, data-agent-kit, perplexity-ask (disabled).\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexlev_oauth\\oauth_flow.py`** — Created and updated 3 times. Final version: Python OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow with HTML redirect, local callback server on port 19876, 10-minute timeout. Saves tokens to `nexlev_tokens.json` in same directory.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.claude.json`** (888 lines) — Massive Claude Code config. Lines 1-753: cached feature flags (skip). Lines 770-786: OAuth account info (Vijay Gorfad, founders@useunitpay.com). Lines 882-887: MCP servers section with nexlev entry `{\"type\":\"http\",\"url\":\"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\"}`. **No OAuth token present yet.**\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\builtin\\skills\\agy-customizations\\docs\\mcp_servers.md`** (87 lines) — MCP config schema. SSE transport uses `serverUrl`, Stdio uses `command`/`args`/`env`. Global config at `~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json`.\n- **`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\builtin\\skills\\agy-customizations\\SKILL.md`** (105 lines) — Customization system overview.\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n### Immediately Check\n**Task `task-184` may have completed or still be running.** The Python OAuth script was launched and the user said they approved. Check:\n1. Read `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\9ecf2b20-4f14-47c7-887d-090725d6fd1c\\.system_generated\\tasks\\task-184.log` for SUCCESS or TIMEOUT\n2. Check if `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexlev_oauth\\nexlev_tokens.json` exists\n\n### If tokens exist (SUCCESS path):\n1. Read the access token from `nexlev_tokens.json`\n2. Build a local MCP proxy bridge (Python, similar to `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\vidiq_bridge\\vidiq_mcp_bridge.py`) that:\n   - Accepts MCP tool calls via stdio\n   - Forwards them to `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n   - Returns results\n3. Update `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\mcp_config.json` to replace the SSE `nexlev` entry with a stdio entry pointing to the bridge\n4. Test by searching for \"stickman animation\" channels (user's suggested test query)\n5. Explain how NexLev helps as a long-form content creator\n\n### If tokens don't exist (TIMEOUT/FAILURE path):\n1. Re-run the OAuth script at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexlev_oauth\\oauth_flow.py`\n2. Tell user to check browser and approve\n3. The user gets frustrated easily — be direct and minimize back-and-forth\n\n### Skills Read\n- `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\builtin\\skills\\agy-customizations\\SKILL.md` — How to configure MCP servers in Antigravity\n- `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\builtin\\skills\\agy-customizations\\docs\\mcp_servers.md` — MCP config schema (SSE vs Stdio transport)\n\nYou have the 9 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787660786217]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9ecf2b20-4f14-47c7-887d-090725d6fd1c/.user_uploaded/media_1787660786217.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-25T12:27:47Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787660873187]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9ecf2b20-4f14-47c7-887d-090725d6fd1c/.user_uploaded/media_1787660873187.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-25T12:28:09Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787661358865]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9ecf2b20-4f14-47c7-887d-090725d6fd1c/.user_uploaded/media_1787661358865.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-25T12:36:23Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787661513966]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9ecf2b20-4f14-47c7-887d-090725d6fd1c/.user_uploaded/media_1787661513966.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-25T12:39:00Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787662132522]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravit