{"step_index":227,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:53:23Z","content":"Now I see! The auth endpoint redirects to `/google/authorize` — NexLev uses **Google OAuth** for login. So the flow is:\n\n1. `auth.nexlev.io/authorize` → redirects to Google login\n2. Google login → redirects back to `auth.nexlev.io` \n3. `auth.nexlev.io` → SHOULD redirect to our `localhost:6274/callback` with a code\n\nBut since you're already logged into Google AND NexLev, it auto-completes steps 1-2 and should redirect to step 3. The fact that it's going to the dashboard instead means the redirect is being lost.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach — **intercept the token from your existing Claude.ai connection** instead:","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"# Try the NexLev API endpoint directly - maybe it works with just cookies/session\n$response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri \"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\" -Method GET -UseBasicParsing -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue 2>&1\nWrite-Host \"STATUS=$($response.StatusCode)\"\nWrite-Host \"CONTENT_TYPE=$($response.Headers.'Content-Type')\"\n$response.Content.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(500, $response.Content.Length))","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\renu5","WaitMsBeforeAsync":15000,"toolAction":"Testing MCP endpoint","toolSummary":"MCP endpoint test"}}]}
{"step_index":228,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:53:39Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T19:23:39+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T19:24:12+05:30\n\nThe command exited with code 1.\nOutput:\nInvoke-WebRequest : {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"error\":{\"code\":-32601,\"message\":\"Method not allowed. This endpoint operates in \r\nstateless mode and only accepts POST requests.\"},\"id\":null}\r\nAt line:2 char:13\r\n+ $response = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri \"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/ ...\r\n+             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n    + CategoryInfo          : InvalidOperation: (System.Net.HttpWebRequest:HttpWebRequest) [Invoke-WebRequest], WebExc \r\n   eption\r\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : WebCmdletWebResponseException,Microsoft.PowerShell.Commands.InvokeWebRequestCommand\r\nSTATUS=\nCONTENT_TYPE=\nYou cannot call a method on a null-valued expression.\r\nAt line:5 char:1\r\n+ $response.Content.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(500, $response.Content.Len ...\r\n+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n    + CategoryInfo          : InvalidOperation: (:) [], RuntimeException\r\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : InvokeMethodOnNull\r\n \r\n\n"}
{"step_index":229,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:54:12Z","content":"Interesting! The MCP endpoint **accepts POST requests and operates in stateless mode**. This means it uses **Streamable HTTP** transport, not SSE. And the error says \"Method not allowed\" — it didn't say \"Unauthorized\"! Let me try a proper MCP request:","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$body = @{\n    jsonrpc = \"2.0\"\n    id = 1\n    method = \"initialize\"\n    params = @{\n        protocolVersion = \"2024-11-05\"\n        capabilities = @{}\n        clientInfo = @{\n            name = \"Antigravity\"\n            version = \"1.0\"\n        }\n    }\n} | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 5\n\ntry {\n    $response = Invoke-RestMethod -Uri \"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\" -Method POST -Body $body -ContentType \"application/json\" -ErrorAction Stop\n    $response | ConvertTo-Json -Depth 10\n} catch {\n    Write-Host \"ERROR: $($_.Exception.Message)\"\n    if ($_.Exception.Response) {\n        $reader = New-Object System.IO.StreamReader($_.Exception.Response.GetResponseStream())\n        Write-Host \"BODY: $($reader.ReadToEnd())\"\n    }\n}","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\renu5","WaitMsBeforeAsync":15000,"toolAction":"Testing MCP initialize","toolSummary":"MCP direct test"}}]}
