{"step_index":233,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:54:46Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"nexlev API key authentication bearer token alternative to OAuth","toolAction":"Searching for API key","toolSummary":"NexLev API key search"}}]}
{"step_index":234,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T13:54:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T19:24:55+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T19:25:02+05:30\nThe search for \"nexlev API key authentication bearer token alternative to OAuth\" returned the following summary:\nFor the **NexLev API**, you are already using a standard and secure method of authentication: **API Key-based Bearer Token authentication**[1][2].\n\nIf you are looking to understand this method or seek alternatives to the full-scale OAuth flow (which NexLev also supports for specific integrations like AI assistants)[3], here is how these authentication patterns compare and function.\n\n### 1. The Current Method: API Key (Bearer Token)\nNexLev provides an **API Key** that you use as a Bearer Token[1][2]. In technical terms, this is a \"stateless\" credential[4][5].\n*   **How it works:** You include the key in the HTTP header of your requests[6][7].\n    *   **Header format:** `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`[2][7]\n*   **Why it is used:** It is significantly simpler than OAuth[8]. It is ideal for server-to-server communication, n8n workflows, or custom scripts where you do not need to delegate access to a third party[9][2][10].\n*   **Security Tip:** Because it is a \"bearer\" token, anyone who possesses it has access to your account[8][7][5]. **Never share your NexLev API key publicly or commit it to version control**[1][11].\n\n### 2. Alternatives to OAuth\nIf you want to avoid the complexity of OAuth (redirects, authorization servers, etc.) while maintaining secure authentication, here are the standard industry alternatives:\n\n| Method | How it works | Best for... |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **API Key (Current)** | A static or semi-static string passed in the header[7]. | Simple scripts, cron jobs, and internal tools[12]. |\n| **JWT (JSON Web Token)** | A self-contained, signed token that can carry user data[5]. | Stateless applications where you want to embed permissions directly in the token[13][10]. |\n| **Basic Authentication** | Sending `username:password` (Base64 encoded) in the header[8][12]. | **Not recommended** for modern APIs due to lower security compared to tokens[4][14]. |\n| **mTLS** | Mutual TLS, which uses client-side certificates for authentication[15]. | High-security, infrastructure-level enterprise requirements[15][10]. |\n\n### Summary Recommendation\n*   **If you are building custom integrations or automations (like in n8n or Python scripts):** Stick with the **API Key Bearer Token** method[1][2]. It is the intended \"non-OAuth\" path for NexLev[9].\n*   **If you need better security without OAuth:** If you are building your own service and find OAuth too heavy, implement **JWTs** (JSON Web Tokens)[10][5]. You can issue these to your clients, and they can pass them as Bearer tokens just like your current API key[16][6].\n\nIf you are currently using NexLev's API documentation, you can continue to use the **API Key** method provided in your dashboard for all REST API operations[9][2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [nexlev.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE0BcicXi7VVbQCBW1VGw0Z1IFre5FRKJdngErJeB85e2Fi-B_iV3nUakn_MiiRaOI4BO4yjl-3htQpasb2d-XjZih1OhMe-sxMf3Nt4VARcjAynLjpXHovQetFTd9nJsZ9Kopr)\n[2] [nexlev.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE4RcxIPdh-a4cle20dQQgmKtWBKd7iDVQMFe_LrYeJn3BHlCNP070GGoJLDsaFLskyacLAtp30t8i9qcrvTFmLt_achQPUDtdIkaIfAcz0-L8m83EghCuEze1_YT9xQKo9mNdTVgBqh3g=)\n[3] [nexlev.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFdfin_s3l80qEAXpjRYrBztF4cf_HUAMMq74DDFNUIw4Zf7sh-XWNNDOkkSqFOeW9-Pmj7mWaqSCumPvZjJRGBshtQ380B8-FbgHyBhXE=)\n[4] [ssojet.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFr71h7ZxulZi7PaUFV1GpFQnCovw4WQGiMgs6xfscpcx2PFchbYoA56RVf-njifmfbIjOQa0vgEpTBBVRXQpOVMEzq2EnjNweaqN8pBj7egzZwTEHVYGdQzxP09l0fo-UzG04pujTEslShqN9lPjdMmno3CqjCwtw8asw16R5Yb08HpZmK