{"step_index":249,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:13:29Z","content":"Here's where we are:\n\n**Done:** Identified NexLev MCP endpoint and how vidIQ bridge works\n**Doing now:** Building a NexLev MCP bridge (same pattern as vidIQ) + registering it in config\n\nLet me build it now:","thinking":"The user wants me to build a NexLev MCP bridge just like the vidIQ one. Let me recap:\n\n1. I have the vidIQ bridge pattern - it's a stdio MCP bridge that proxies requests to the remote MCP endpoint\n2. NexLev MCP endpoint: `https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp` (requires auth)\n3. The NexLev MCP uses OAuth, but NexLev also has a REST API with API keys\n\nThe user said \"not api is required\" - I think they mean the NexLev API section on dashboard has an API key they can use. \n\nI'm reconsidering though - the NexLev MCP endpoint itself likely requires OAuth tokens, while the separate REST API uses API keys, so these might not be interchangeable. I recall from earlier search results that NexLev does offer an API key option somewhere in their dashboard.\n\nI'll go ahead and build the bridge now, following the same pattern as vidIQ: proxying to NexLev's Claude-specific MCP endpoint with a Bearer token, requiring the user to supply their own API key.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nNexLev MCP Bridge — Stdio proxy to NexLev's remote MCP endpoint.\nSame pattern as the vidIQ bridge. Reads API key from mcp_config.json.\nAuto-discovers all 74 NexLev tools from the remote server.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport asyncio\nimport aiohttp\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom mcp.server.stdio import stdio_server\nfrom mcp.server import Server\nfrom mcp.types import Tool, TextContent\n\n# --- Configuration ---\nNEXLEV_MCP_URL = \"https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp\"\n\nCONFIG_PATHS = [\n    Path(os.path.expanduser(\"~\")) / \".gemini\" / \"config\" / \"mcp_config.json\",\n]\n\nlocal_server = Server(\"nexlev-mcp-bridge\")\n\n# --- Session State ---\n_remote_tools = None\n_http_session = None\n_request_counter = 0\n_current_api_key = None\n_initialized = False\n\n\ndef _next_id():\n    global _request_counter\n    _request_counter += 1\n    return _request_counter\n\n\ndef _read_api_key():\n    \"\"\"Read the NexLev API key from config file or env var.\"\"\"\n    for config_path in CONFIG_PATHS:\n        try:\n            if config_path.exists():\n                with open(config_path, \"r\") as f:\n                    config = json.load(f)\n                servers = config.get(\"mcpServers\", {})\n                nexlev = servers.get(\"nexlev\", {})\n                env = nexlev.get(\"env\", {})\n                key = env.get(\"NEXLEV_API_KEY\", \"\")\n                if key:\n                    return key\n        except Exception:\n            continue\n    return os.environ.get(\"NEXLEV_API_KEY\", \"\")\n\n\ndef _get_headers():\n    \"\"\"Build headers with API key as Bearer token.\"\"\"\n    api_key = _read_api_key()\n    headers = {\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n        \"Accept\": \"application/json, text/event-stream\",\n    }\n    if api_key:\n        headers[\"Authorization\"] = f\"Bearer {api_key}\"\n    return headers\n\n\ndef _parse_sse_sync(text):\n    \"\"\"Parse SSE response text and return the JSON-RPC result.\"\"\"\n    for line in text.split(\"\\n\"):\n        line = line.strip()\n        if line.startswith(\"data:\"):\n            data_str = line[5:].strip()\n            if data_str:\n                try:\n                    return json.loads(data_str)\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    continue\n    return None\n\n\nasync def _parse_response(response):\n    \"\"\"Parse response — handles both JSON and SSE formats.\"\"\"\n    content_type = response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\", \"\")\n    if \"text/event-stream\" in content_type:\n        text = await response.text()\n        return _parse_sse_sync(text)\n    else:\n        return await response.json()\n\n\ndef _invalidate():\n    \"\"\"Reset all state.\"\"\"\n    global _remote_tools, _current_api_key, _initialized\n    _remote_tools = None\n    _current_api_key = None\n    _initialized = False\n\n\nasync def _get_session():\n    \"\"\"Get or create HTTP session.\"\"\"\n    global _http_session\n    if _http_session is None or _http_session.closed:\n        _http_session = aiohttp.ClientSession()\n    return _http_session\n\n\nasync def _init_and_discover():\n    \"\"\"Initialize connection and discover tools.\"\"\"\n    global _remote_tools, _current_api_key, _initialized\n\n    current_key = _read_api_key()\n    if not current_key:\n        raise Exception(\n            \"No API key. Set NEXLEV_API_KEY in ~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json under nexlev.env\"\n        )\n\n    if _initialized and current_key == _current_api_key:\n        return\n\n    _invalidate()\n    _current_api_key = current_key\n    session = await _get_session()\n    headers = _get_headers()\n\n    # Step 1: Initialize\n    init_req = {\n        \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n        \"id\": _next_id(),\n        \"method\": \"initialize\",\n        \"params\": {\n            \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-03-26\",\n            \"capabilities\": {},\n            \"clientInfo\": {\"name\": \"nexlev-mcp-bridge\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\"}\n        }\n    }\n\n    try:\n        async with session.post(\n            NEXLEV_MCP_URL, headers=headers, json=init_req,\n            timeout=aiohttp.ClientTimeout(total=30)\n        ) as resp:\n            if resp.status == 401:\n                _invalidate()\n                raise Exception(\"API key rejected (401). Update NEXLEV_API_KEY in mcp_config.json\")\n            if resp.status != 200:\n                _invalidate()\n                text = await resp.text()\n                raise Exception(f\"Init failed: HTTP {resp.status} - {text}\")\n            await _parse_response(resp)\n    except (aiohttp.ClientError, asyncio.TimeoutError) as e:\n        _invalidate()\n        raise Exception(f\"Connection failed: {e}\")\n\n    # Step 2: Initialized notification\n    try:\n        async with session.post(\n            NEXLEV_MCP_URL, headers=headers,\n            json={\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": \"notifications/initialized\", \"params\": {}},\n            timeout=aiohttp.ClientTimeout(total=10)\n        ) as resp:\n            pass\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    # Step 3: Discover tools\n    try:\n        async with session.post(\n            NEXLEV_MCP_URL, headers=headers,\n            json={\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": _next_id(), \"method\": \"tools/list\", \"params\": {}},\n            timeout=aiohttp.ClientTimeout(total=30)\n        ) as resp:\n            if resp.status == 200:\n                result = await _parse_response(resp)\n                if result and \"result\" in result:\n                    tools_data = result[\"result\"]\n                    if isinstance(tools_data, dict) and \"tools\" in tools_data:\n                        _remote_tools = tools_data[\"tools\"]\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    _initialized = True\n\n\n# --- Fallback hardcoded tool list (core NexLev tools) ---\nNEXLEV_TOOLS = [\n    Tool(name=\"find_long_form_channels\", description=\"Find long-form YouTube channels by niche, size, and growth rate\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Search query or niche\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"find_shorts_channels\", description=\"Find Shorts-only channels by niche, engagement, and upload frequency\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Search query or niche\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_similar_channels\", description=\"Discover channels with overlapping audience and content style\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube channel ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"channel_resolver\", description=\"Resolve any channel ID, handle, custom URL, or alias to a canonical ID\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Channel handle, URL, or ID\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_channel_analytics\", description=\"Full channel snapshot — subscribers, views, revenue, and upload pace\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube channel ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_daily_analytics\", description=\"Daily performance trends and growth tracking for any channel\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube channel ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_geography_revenue\", description=\"Revenue estimates, RPM by country, and geographic demographics\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube channel ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"batch_channel_metrics\", description=\"Compare up to 10 channels side-by-side in a single request\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_ids\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Comma-separated channel IDs\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_ids\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"search_youtube_suggested_videos\", description=\"Search YouTube suggested videos with outlier scores and engagement filters\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Search query\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"search_viral_videos_small_channels\", description=\"Find breakout hits from low-subscriber channels\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Search query or niche\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_similar_videos\", description=\"Find videos similar to any input by content match and engagement\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"video_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube video ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"video_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"youtube_search\", description=\"General YouTube search across videos, channels, and playlists\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Search query\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"youtube_video_details\", description=\"Fetch full metadata and statistics for any YouTube video\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"video_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube video ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"video_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"youtube_video_comments\", description=\"Retrieve top comments from any YouTube video\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"video_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube video ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"video_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_video_transcript\", description=\"Get the full transcript of any YouTube video\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"video_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube video ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"video_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_niche_overview\", description=\"Audience profile, content formats, and brand fit for any niche\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"niche\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Niche name\"}}, \"required\": [\"niche\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"check_channel_monetization\", description=\"Check monetization eligibility and brand deal signals\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube channel ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"get_video_rpm\", description=\"Get estimated RPM and revenue data for any YouTube video\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"video_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube video ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"video_id\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"similar_thumbnails\", description=\"Search and compare thumbnails across millions of YouTube videos\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"query\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Search query or video URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"query\"]}),\n    Tool(name=\"latest_discovered_faceless_niches\", description=\"Find top-performing faceless or AI-generated channels in any niche\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {}, \"required\": []}),\n    Tool(name=\"check_faceless_channel\", description=\"Verify whether a specific channel uses faceless or AI-driven content\", inputSchema={\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"channel_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"YouTube channel ID or URL\"}}, \"required\": [\"channel_id\"]}),\n]\n\n\n@local_server.list_tools()\nasync def handle_list_tools() -> list[Tool]:\n    try:\n        await _init_and_discover()\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    if _remote_tools:\n        return [\n            Tool(\n                name=t.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n                description=t.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n                inputSchema=t.get(\"inputSchema\", {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {}, \"required\": []})\n            )\n            for t in _remote_tools\n        ]\n    return NEXLEV_TOOLS\n\n\n@local_server.call_tool()\nasync def handle_call_tool(name: str, arguments: dict) -> list[TextContent]:\n    for attempt in range(2):\n        try:\n            await _init_and_discover()\n        except Exception as e:\n            return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=f\"Error: {e}\")]\n\n        session = await _get_session()\n        headers = _get_headers()\n\n        call_request = {\n            \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n            \"id\": _next_id(),\n            \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n            \"params\": {\"name\": name, \"arguments\": arguments}\n        }\n\n        try:\n            async with session.post(\n                NEXLEV_MCP_URL, headers=headers, json=call_request,\n                timeout=aiohttp.ClientTimeout(total=60)\n            ) as response:\n                if response.status == 401:\n                    _invalidate()\n                    if attempt == 0:\n                        continue\n                    return [TextContent(\n                        type=\"text\",\n                        text=\"Error: API key rejected (401). Update NEXLEV_API_KEY in mcp_config.json\"\n                    )]\n\n                if response.status != 200:\n                    text = await response.text()\n                    if attempt == 0:\n                        _invalidate()\n                        continue\n                    return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=f\"Error: HTTP {response.status} - {text}\")]\n\n                result = await _parse_response(response)\n\n                if result is None:\n                    return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=\"Error: Empty response from NexLev\")]\n\n                if \"error\" in result:\n                    error = result[\"error\"]\n                    return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=f\"NexLev error: {error.get('message', str(error))}\")]\n\n                if \"result\" in result:\n                    content = result[\"result\"]\n                    if isinstance(content, dict) and \"content\" in content:\n                        texts = []\n                        for item in content[\"content\"]:\n                            if isinstance(item, dict) and item.get(\"type\") == \"text\":\n                                texts.append(item.get(\"text\", \"\"))\n                            else:\n                                texts.append(json.dumps(item, indent=2))\n                        return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=\"\\n\".join(texts))]\n                    else:\n                        return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=json.dumps(content, indent=2))]\n\n                return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=json.dumps(result, indent=2))]\n\n        except asyncio.TimeoutError:\n            return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=\"Error: Request timed out (60s). Try again.\")]\n        except aiohttp.ClientError as e:\n            _invalidate()\n            if attempt == 0:\n                continue\n            return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=f\"Error: Connection failed - {e}\")]\n        except Exception as e:\n            return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=f\"Error: {type(e).__name__} - {e}\")]\n\n    return [TextContent(type=\"text\", text=\"Error: Failed after 2 attempts.\")]\n\n\nasync def main():\n    async with stdio_server() as (read_stream, write_stream):\n        await local_server.run(read_stream, write_stream, local_server.create_initialization_options())\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(main())\n","Description":"NexLev MCP bridge using same pattern as vidIQ - stdio proxy to remote NexLev MCP endpoint with Bearer token auth","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\nexlev_bridge\\nexlev_mcp_bridge.py","toolAction":"Creating NexLev bridge","toolSummary":"NexLev MCP bridge"}}]}
